.TH LINKWISE-STATION 5 "2026-11-12" "Linkwise" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
linkwise\-station \- Linkwise modem station configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I station.json
.SH DESCRIPTION
The station configuration is a UTF-8 JSON object.
The file is limited to 16 KiB.
Unknown keys are rejected.
.BR linkwise-modemd (8)
reads the file specified on its command line.
.SH FIELDS
.TP
.B version
Required integer.
Use 1 for this format.
.TP
.B callsign
Required station callsign.
Linkwise trims whitespace and converts letters to uppercase.
.TP
.BR input ", " output
Required objects with a
.B name
string and a zero-based integer
.B channel .
Use the exact device names reported by
.BR "linkwise-modemd --audio-devices" .
.TP
.B bandwidth
Optional integer in Hz.
Use 500, 2300, or 2750 for two-way native audio.
Omit this field to run receive diagnostics.
.TP
.BR command_port ", " data_port
Optional TCP ports.
The defaults are 8300 and 8301 respectively.
Choose distinct nonzero port numbers.
Only the command port is used for receive diagnostics.
For Winlink Express, use the command port followed by the next consecutive
port for data.
.TP
.B bw500_profile
Path to a BW500 measurement profile in JSON, limited to 128 KiB.
Relative paths are resolved from the station file's directory.
The field is required for two-way operation at 500 Hz and optional for
receive diagnostics.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/linkwise/station.json
Linux system service configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.config/linkwise/station.json
Linux user service configuration.
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/Linkwise/station.json
macOS login agent configuration.
.SH EXAMPLES
A two-way 500 Hz station configuration follows.
Replace the callsign, device names, and profile path with those for your
station.
.EX
{
  "version": 1,
  "callsign": "W1AW",
  "input": {"name": "Radio input", "channel": 0},
  "output": {"name": "Radio output", "channel": 0},
  "bandwidth": 500,
  "bw500_profile": "bw500-profile.json"
}
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR linkwise-modemd (8)
